                <pb facs="0227" n="125" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg125"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">704.2523: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Shea</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-11-28T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 28,
                                1918, 4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            November 29, 1.20 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Minister of Foreign Affairs requested me today to ask that United States consular
                    officers in Peru be placed in charge of Chilean consular interests. Instructions
                    desired. Strongly urge that this be done if consistent with policy.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Shea</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
